-- title:
--   Hecke-balanced pairing with multiplicative-type left kernel (q odd)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq 2$ and $q \neq p$, and let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ lying in its nonunits. The module $J_0(p) := \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ carries the Hecke action of $\mathbb{T} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ given by `heckeModuleBar p`. Write $I = \mathrm{span}\{q^k\} + \mathfrak{m}^M$, where $\mathfrak{m} =$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` is the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of $(q) \subset \mathbb{Z}$, and $V =$ the submodule of $J_0(p)$ annihilated by $I$. Let $R$ be the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra of endomorphisms of the integral lattice in weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(p)$ generated by the Hecke operators, $\varphi : \mathbb{T} \to R$ the map sending $X_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ or $T_\ell$ according as $\ell \mid p$ or not, and $J = \mathrm{span}\{q^k\} + (\varphi(\mathfrak{m})R)^M$. Then for all $k, M \in \mathbb{N}$ and every $n : \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathbb{N}$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{n(\sigma)}$ for all $\sigma$ and all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{q^k} = 1$, assuming the two stabilisation hypotheses that the $I$-torsion of $J_0(p)$ is unchanged on replacing $M$ by $M+1$ and likewise for the ideal $J$ of $R$, the following holds: for every Hecke submodule $W \le J_0(p)$ of multiplicative type, i.e. $\sigma \cdot x = n(\sigma)\, x$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A_q$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and all $x \in W$, which contains every multiplicative-type submodule of $V$, there is a map $e : V \times (R/J) \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^\times$ additive-to-multiplicative in each variable, satisfying $e(t \cdot v, r) = e(v, \varphi(t)r)$ for $t \in \mathbb{T}$, with $e(\cdot, r) \equiv 1$ only for $r = 0$, and with $e(v, \cdot) \equiv 1$ exactly when $v \in W$.
--
--   This is the Cartier-type duality of Mazur's study of the Eisenstein ideal, in the form of a Hecke-balanced pairing between the $q$-power Eisenstein torsion of $J_0(p)$ and the corresponding quotient of the Hecke lattice algebra, whose left kernel is the maximal submodule of multiplicative type. It is used in the construction of that multiplicative-type submodule together with its pairing, the inputs being the two characterisations of multiplicative type in terms of the Hecke lattice algebra and the existence of a generating character on the Eisenstein torsion.
